# BMW 7 Series E23 four-door saloon, 1977-1986.
#
# The first 7-series: a long, low four-door with quad round headlamps, built to
# replace the E3 "New Six" and sold in Britain from 1977 as the 728, 730 and
# 733i, later the 728i, 732i and 735i.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BMW_7_Series_(E23)
# https://www.motorsportmagazine.com/archive/article/september-1977/65/the-bmw-7-series/
#
# Dimensions 4.860 x 1.800 x 1.430 m, wheelbase 2.795 m, European
# specification, from the English Wikipedia dimension box which cites Auto Motor
# und Sport 11/1977. The North American car is 5,014 mm on its impact bumpers.
# Mirrors take the modelled width to 1.919 m.
#
# The pre-facelift car is modelled, 1977-1982: narrow separate kidneys and the
# earlier front. The September 1982 facelift widened the kidneys, added a front
# air dam and changed the lamp clusters; that nose is not represented, and the
# reference photographs of the facelift car were used only for rear lamp
# placement and boot shape. The US-market side photograph's 5 mph bumpers and
# side marker lights are deliberately not modelled: the UK car had slim
# bumpers.
#
# Colours. No UK colour card for the E23 was located; these are BMW programme
# colours of the period from an aftermarket paint-code reference, so the names
# are established BMW finishes but UK availability is probable rather than
# proven:
#   Alpinweiss              146, c.1977-1986
#   Schwarz                 086, 1977-1986
#   Polaris metallic        060, 1977-1981 (New Polaris to 1986)
#   Saphirblau metallic     149, 1980-1984
# Saphirblau therefore starts in 1980. Weights silver 3, black 3, blue 2,
# white 2, total 10, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 212 km/h, the 735i's quoted maximum and the 733i's as well. Comfort
# 130/375, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 130, a step below the E32's 140/390.
# Class 4, the top wealth band, as the other 7-series cars are.
#
# Dates are road presence, not production: May 1977 intro, retires staggered
# 1997-2000 on a fourteen- to seventeen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/bmw-e23.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/bmw-e23.dae (75 objects). References:
# citycars/references/bmw-e23/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted low-poly deviations, recorded rather than corrected: the body
# surfaces are flatter than the photographs and the lower corners are squared.
# At 128 px the long bonnet, upright cabin and quad lamps read correctly.

